From 95c202243d54a1a453ba3433dde1e076f0f2d939 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin <justurn@live.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Apr 2026 00:49:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(DB): Split 00_cleanup.sql across db-world and
 db-characters (I-171)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The original cleanup file used `USE acore_characters;` mid-file to
DELETE from character_settings after doing world DB cleanup. This
required the apply user to have grants on both databases — if the
apply user lacks privilege on acore_characters, the world-DB apply
fails entirely with access-denied.

Split the characters DELETE into its own file under
db-characters/base/00_cleanup.sql so it's routed to the right DB with
the right credentials by the apply tooling, and the world cleanup
stays purely world.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 data/sql/db-characters/base/00_cleanup.sql | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 data/sql/db-characters/base/00_cleanup.sql

diff --git a/data/sql/db-characters/base/00_cleanup.sql b/data/sql/db-characters/base/00_cleanup.sql
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..50b3361
--- /dev/null
+++ b/data/sql/db-characters/base/00_cleanup.sql
@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@
+-- Cleanup for mod-individual-progression settings
+-- Split out of db-world/base/00_cleanup.sql — cross-DB SQL in a single
+-- file required acore user to have grants on both databases (I-171).
+
+DELETE FROM `character_settings` WHERE `source` = 'mod-individual-progression';
-- 
2.34.1

